  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - This development shall be begun within 3 years from the date of this permission.\r\nTo comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990.\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved drawings and specifications,\r\nunless approved otherwise in writing by the local planning authority.  \r\nTo ensure a satisfactory standard of development, and to allow the local planning authority to review any potential changes to the scheme.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - REASON FOR GRANTING PLANNING PERMISSION\r\nThe Council has had regard to local development plan policies, to any representations received and to other material planning considerations. \r\nThe following policies were considered relevant to the grant of planning permission: DMPD Submission Version (May 2011): Policies DMS1 (Sustainable design), DMS2 (Managing the historic environment), DMC2 (Community facilities), UDP (2003): TBE5 (Design and external appearance); TBE10 (Conservation Areas), CS3 (Education and childcare facilities), PPS5\r\nThe proposal has been granted planning permission for the following reasons:\r\nThe design of the additions would be in keeping with the character and appearance of the existing building and the conservation area; and the proposal would not have an adverse impact on the amenity of the neighbouring properties in terms of loss of light, privacy and outlook"
  ]
